.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-LEAVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-leave - Leave a team


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team leave <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Leave a team yourself. An owner must transfer ownership first (pb team transfer) before
leaving.
Pass the team's current generation with --generation (read it with pb team get). A stale
generation is rejected, so two people editing the team never overwrite each other.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--generation\fP=0
	expected current team generation

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for leave

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team leave acme --generation 9
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
